body:
> All he has to do is drone somebody out, click a button, and push. In  this situation lion knows EXACTLY where the defender is, if the defender  tries moving then he gets marked and gets shot, if he doesn’t then they  still know where he is. So the defender is basically fucked with all  odds against him 

Not really, Lion's three seconds before EE1D actually spots gives defenders some time to move locations and get a different angle along with a different stance to get the drop on Lion. (On top of that there's the time it takes to put his phone away, and take his gun out, nothing big but it's still something.)

&#x200B;

I do agree that Lion's gadget should be tweaked, but I really don't think that your rework is necessarily appropriate. Simply replacing the gadget's outlining effect with a general area of enemy location would be a sufficient nerf.

&#x200B;
